course: dictionary
lesson: 4361
title: Gunk: sticky, dirty mess
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Gunk» is an informal word, so you will hear it in everyday talk and funny stories about mess more often than in formal writing. Its clues are in the sentence around it. «Waking up with your eyes glued shut by yellow gunk» tells you the stuff is sticky, because it glues things shut, and it is dirty, because it is yellow and not wanted.
explain: Try the swap test. Put your meaning in place of the word: «...your eyes glued shut by yellow sticky dirty stuff» still makes sense, so your meaning is probably right. Check the clues again if it doesn't.
explain: Gunk can be grease in a drain or goo on a shoe. Phrases help too. «Full of gunk» means full of thick dirty stuff. «Clean the gunk out» means remove it. «Gunk up» means to block something with gunk.
fact: «Gunk» is an informal noun, so it is used in everyday talk and funny stories more than in formal writing.
fact: «Gunk» means thick, sticky, dirty or slimy stuff that you do not want.
fact: «Gunk» is uncountable: you say «some gunk», not «a gunk» or «two gunks».
fact: Phrases with gunk: «full of gunk», «clean the gunk out», and «gunk up», which means to block something with gunk.
fact: Examples of gunk include grease in a drain and goo on a shoe.
exercise: «Waking up with your eyes glued shut by yellow gunk is usually conjunctivitis, pink eye.» What is the gunk? | *A thick, sticky, dirty stuff | A type of bird | A bright, shiny toy | A kind of cloud
exercise: The kitchen drain is full of gunk. What does «gunk up» mean? | To wash your hands very fast | *To block with thick, dirty stuff | To shine a light on something | To play a loud game
exercise: Mum says, «Clean the gunk out of the sink.» What must you do? | Fill the sink with sweets | Put the sink on a high shelf | Sing a song to the sink | *Remove the thick, dirty stuff from the sink
test: «Waking up with your eyes glued shut by yellow gunk is usually conjunctivitis, pink eye.» What does «glued shut» tell you about the gunk? | It is dry and light | It is invisible | It is hot and steaming | *It is sticky
test: We say «some gunk», not «a gunk». Why? | *Gunk is uncountable, so you cannot count it as one or two | Gunk is a plural word with no singular | Gunk is always stored in a box | Gunk is a name for a person
exam: «The shoe was covered in gunk.» Which meaning fits best? | A tiny insect | A sweet pudding | *A dirty, sticky mess | A clean, shining polish
